ImportFinding.description:
One actionable observation. blocking must be fixed by an edit;
review_required needs a teacher decision (an edit or an acknowledgement);
informational needs nothing.

AiScoreSuggestion.description:
`score` is one of the multiples of 0.5 from 0 to the question's points:
what the model proposed is moved to the nearest one. Nothing is saved;
a teacher marks the answer with `gradeAttempt`.

Set-Cookie.description:
Two headers. `quizzivy_refresh=; Max-Age=0` with the same Path and flags,
or the browser keeps the old cookie; and `quizzivy_docs=; Path=/docs;
Max-Age=0`, so signing out also ends an open API reference session (§5.5).

post.description:
Starts processing an import awaiting sources, retries a failed one, or
reprocesses one under review. Reprocessing never replaces teacher edits;
the new result is offered in the review instead.

parameters.description:
Only students who are in at least one of these classes (`classId=a&classId=b`;
one value still works). A class the caller does not reach matches nothing,
as a missing class does.
